{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 10790490841992965066, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 632, "mtime": 1791872054.9996934, "sha256": "43e56f6172c61918dffe9711cb4ebb35db41b2801606cc03024531a297d63c95"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 466, "mtime": 1791872057.9399061, "sha256": "dc0a4d8c6ae9b3a60603d5fa7197bc4dae4a89ac1ae5048cd7fc698652752ba9"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/15/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/15/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running the suite.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. The new tests pass and so does the existing `test_split`. I couldn't use pytest because it isn't installed, so I ran the test functions directly with `python3`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. `round()` also rounds halves to the nearest even digit (`round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`), which is not the \"half up\" rule the docstring promises.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now converts the number with `Decimal(repr(x))`, which gives the exact value `2.675`, and rounds that to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. It still returns a float, so `add_vat` and other callers don't change. Negative halves round away from zero (`-2.675` \u2192 `-2.68`).\n\n**Regression test:** `tests/test_round_money.py` checks `2.675` \u2192 `2.68`, `1.005` \u2192 `1.01`, `0.125` \u2192 `0.13` and the negative case. Plain `round()` gives `2.67`, `1.0` and `0.12` for the first three, so these tests would have caught the bug.\n\nOne limit: this rounds the float exactly as it arrives. If arithmetic before the call has already produced something like `2.6749999999999998`, it will still round down. For example, `add_vat` multiplies before rounding, so it could hit this. Fully avoiding that would mean doing the price maths in `Decimal` from the start, which is a bigger change I didn't make.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 246210, "requests_cache_write": 15399, "requests_cost_usd": 0.172157, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2292, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude